## Problem classes

### `Vpn overlay classified as Other`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| AUTO flaps PROXY↔VPN when VPN is up | `activeNetwork` is `TRANSPORT_VPN` | Strip our VPN; classify underlying Wi-Fi/cell/other |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Split-brain node`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Same node ID, two paths, peers confused | libzt and JNI both opened `identity.secret` | Mutex; `stopAndAwait()` until peer service `isRunning` false; never two live nodes |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `HTTP_PROXY survives PROXY→VPN swap`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Global still loopback after VPN up | Stopped proxy before `disable()` | `SystemProxyManager.disable()` then `ProxyModeService.stopAndAwait()` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Stack swap races`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Orchestrator starts JNI while libzt still up | Service `shutdown()` has no completion callback | Companion `stopAndAwait()` polls `StateFlow.isRunning` (10s timeout) |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Equal plan re-swap`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| AUTO WiFi A PROXY → WiFi B PROXY triggers stack churn | Re-applied identical `RuntimePlan` | `if (plan == lastApplied) return` before stop/start |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Consent fallback still carries vpnNetworkId`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| UI/services act on VPN id while runtime is PROXY | Consent path set `vpnNetworkId` before downgrade | Set `vpnNetworkId` only when `runtime == VPN` |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->
